# Isolation Level Results

## What Session 1 Observed
In `READ COMMITTED`, Session 1 sees the latest committed row version at the moment each statement is executed. If Session 2 updates the row and commits, Session 1 may see the new value on a later read within the same transaction.

## What Session 2 Changed
Session 2 updates the row and commits the change. This creates a new committed version of the row visible to subsequent statements.

## Why the Behavior Differs
`READ COMMITTED` re-evaluates the row version for each statement, while `REPEATABLE READ` preserves the row snapshot taken at the start of the transaction. As a result, `REPEATABLE READ` prevents later reads from seeing a different committed version within the same transaction.

